msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You work with Quarkus extensions that do not support `HTTP`, such as "
"`Quarkus GRPC`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You provide an extension-specific `HTTP`, the support of which conflicts "
"with the support of those offered by `quarkus-smallrye-jwt` and `Vert.x "
"HTTP`, such as `Quarkus AWS Lambda`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Start with adding the `smallrye-jwt` dependency:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then, update `application.properties` to get all the CDI producers provided "
"by `smallrye-jwt` included as follows:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuration reference"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid "MicroProfile JWT configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid "Property Name"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default"
msgstr ""

msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "none"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `mp.jwt.verify.publickey` config property allows the public key text to "
"be supplied as a string. The public key is parsed from the supplied string "
"in the order defined in the <<supported-public-key-formats>> section."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Config property allows for a specified external or internal location of the "
"public key. The value can be a relative path or a URL. If the value points "
"to an HTTPS-based JWK set, then, for it to work in native mode, the `quarkus."
"ssl.native` property must also be set to `true`. See xref:native-and-ssl."
"adoc[Using SSL With Native Executables] for more details."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.verify.publickey.algorithm`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`RS256`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"List of signature algorithms. Set it to `ES256` to support the Elliptic "
"Curve signature algorithm."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Config property allows for a specified external or internal location of the "
"Private Decryption Key."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.decrypt.key.algorithm`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`RSA-OAEP`,`RSA-OAEP-256`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"List of decryption algorithms. Set it to `RSA-OAEP-256` to support RSA-OAEP "
"with SHA-256 only."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.verify.issuer`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Config property specifies the value of the `iss` (issuer) claim of the JWT "
"that the server accepts as valid."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.verify.audiences`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Comma-separated list of audiences a token `aud` claim might contain."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.verify.clock.skew`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`60`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clock skew in seconds used during the token expiration and age verification. "
"An expired token is accepted if the current time is within the number of "
"seconds specified by this property after the token expiration time. The "
"default value is 60 seconds."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.verify.token.age`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`none`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Number of seconds that must not elapse since the token `iat` (issued at) "
"time."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.token.header`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`Authorization`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set this property if another header, such as `Cookie`, is used to pass the "
"token."
msgstr ""

msgid "`mp.jwt.token.cookie`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Name of the cookie containing a token. This property is effective only if "
"`mp.jwt.token.header` is set to `Cookie`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Additional SmallRye JWT configuration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"SmallRye JWT provides more properties that can be used to customize the "
"token processing:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.secretkey`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Secret key supplied as a string."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.key.location`"
msgstr ""

msgid "NONE"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Location of the verification key, which can point to both public and secret "
"keys. Secret keys can only be in the JWK format. Note that 'mp.jwt.verify."
"publickey.location' is ignored if this property is set."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.algorithm`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Signature algorithm. This property should only be used to set a symmetric "
"algorithm such as `HS256`. It is deprecated for setting asymmetric "
"algorithms such as `ES256` - use 'mp.jwt.verify.publickey.algorithm' instead."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.key-format`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`ANY`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set this property to a specific key format such as `PEM_KEY`, "
"`PEM_CERTIFICATE`, `JWK` or `JWK_BASE64URL` to optimize the way the "
"verification key is loaded."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.key-provider`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`DEFAULT`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, PEM, JWK, or JWK key sets can be read from the local file system "
"or fetched from URIs as required by MicroProfile JWT specification. Set this "
"property to `AWS_ALB` to support an AWS Application Load Balancer "
"verification key resolution."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.relax-key-validation`"
msgstr ""

msgid "false"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Relax the validation of the verification keys; setting this property to "
"`true` allows public RSA keys with a length of less than 2048 bits."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.certificate-thumbprint`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If this property is enabled, a signed token must contain either 'x5t' or "
"'x5t#S256' X509Certificate thumbprint headers. Verification keys can only be "
"in JWK or PEM Certificate key formats. JWK keys must have an 'x5c' (Base64-"
"encoded X509Certificate) property set."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.token.header`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set this property if another header, such as `Cookie`, is used to pass the "
"token. This property is deprecated - use 'mp.jwt.token.header'."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.key-cache-size`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`100`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Key cache size. Use this property and `smallrye.jwt.key-cache-time-to-live` "
"to control the key cache when a key provider such as `AWS_ALB` is configured "
"with `smallrye.jwt.verify.key-provider=AWS_ALB` for resolving the keys "
"dynamically."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.key-cache-time-to-live`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`10`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Key cache entry time-to-live in minutes. Use this property and `smallrye.jwt."
"key-cache-size` to control the key cache when a key provider such as "
"`AWS_ALB` is configured with `smallrye.jwt.verify.key-provider=AWS_ALB` for "
"resolving the keys dynamically."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.token.cookie`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Name of the cookie containing a token. This property is effective only if "
"`smallrye.jwt.token.header` is set to `Cookie`. This property is deprecated -"
" use `mp.jwt.token.cookie`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.always-check-authorization`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set this property to `true` for the `Authorization` header to be checked "
"even if the `smallrye.jwt.token.header` is set to `Cookie` but no cookie "
"with a `smallrye.jwt.token.cookie` name exists."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.token.schemes`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`Bearer`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Comma-separated list containing alternative single or multiple schemes, such "
"as `DPoP`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.token.kid`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Key identifier. The verification JWK key and every JWT token must have a "
"matching `kid` header if it is set."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.time-to-live`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The maximum number of seconds a JWT can be issued for use. Effectively, the "
"difference between the expiration date of the JWT and the issued at date "
"must not exceed this value. Setting this property to a non-positive value "
"relaxes the requirement for the token to have a valid 'iat' (issued at) "
"claim."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.require.named-principal`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`true`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If an application relies on `java.security.Principal` returning a name, then "
"a token must have a `upn` or `preferred_username` or `sub` claim set. "
"Setting this property results in SmallRye JWT throwing an exception if none "
"of these claims is available for the application code to deal with a non-"
"null `Principal` name reliably."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.path.sub`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Path to the claim containing the subject name. It starts from the top-level "
"JSON object and can contain multiple segments where each segment only "
"represents a JSON object name, for example, `realms/subject`. This property "
"can be used if a token has no 'sub' claim but has the subject set in a "
"different claim. Use double quotes with the namespace-qualified claims."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.claims.sub`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This property can set a default sub claim value when the current token has "
"no standard or custom `sub` claim available. Effectively, this property can "
"be used to customize the `java.security.Principal` name if no `upn` or "
"`preferred_username` or `sub` claim is set."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.path.groups`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Path to the claim containing the groups. It starts from the top-level JSON "
"object and can contain multiple segments where each segment represents a "
"JSON object name only, for example: `realm/groups`. This property can be "
"used if a token has no 'groups' claim but has the groups set in a different "
"claim. Use double quotes with the namespace-qualified claims."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.groups-separator`"
msgstr ""

msgid "space"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Separator for splitting a string which might contain multiple group values. "
"It is only used if the `smallrye.jwt.path.groups` property points to a "
"custom claim with a string value. The default value is a single space "
"because a standard OAuth2 `scope` claim might contain a space-separated "
"sequence."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.claims.groups`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This property can set a default groups claim value when the current token "
"has no standard or custom groups claim available."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.jwks.refresh-interval`"
msgstr ""

msgid "60"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"JWK cache refresh interval in minutes. It is ignored unless the `mp.jwt."
"verify.publickey.location` points to the HTTP or HTTPS URL-based JWK set and "
"no HTTP `Cache-Control` response header with a positive `max-age` parameter "
"value is returned from a JWK HTTPS endpoint."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.jwks.forced-refresh-interval`"
msgstr ""

msgid "30"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Forced JWK cache refresh interval in minutes, which is used to restrict the "
"frequency of the forced refresh attempts that might happen when the token "
"verification fails due to the cache having no JWK key with a `kid` property "
"matching the current token's `kid` header. It is ignored unless the `mp.jwt."
"verify.publickey.location` points to the HTTP or HTTPS URL-based JWK set."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.expiration.grace`"
msgstr ""

msgid "0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Expiration grace in seconds. By default, an expired token is still accepted "
"if the current time is no more than 1 min after the token expiry time. This "
"property is deprecated. Use `mp.jwt.verify.clock.skew` instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.verify.aud`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Comma-separated list of audiences a token `aud` claim might contain. This "
"property is deprecated - use `mp.jwt.verify.audiences`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.required.claims`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Comma-separated list of the claims a token must contain."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.decrypt.key.location`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Config property to specify the external or internal location of Private "
"Decryption Key. This property is deprecated - use `mp.jwt.decrypt.key."
"location`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.decrypt.algorithm`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`RSA_OAEP`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Decryption algorithm."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.decrypt.key`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Decryption key supplied as a string."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.token.decryption.kid`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Decryption Key identifier. If it is set then the decryption JWK key as well "
"every JWT token must have a matching `kid` header."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.client.tls.certificate.path`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Path to TLS trusted certificate which might need to be configured if the "
"keys have to be fetched over `HTTPS`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.client.tls.trust-all`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Trust all the hostnames. If the keys have to be fetched over `HTTPS` and "
"this property is set to `true` then all the hostnames are trusted by default."
""
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.client.tls.hosts`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set of trusted hostnames. If the keys have to be fetched over `HTTPS` and "
"`smallrye.jwt.client.tls.trust-all` is set to `false` then this property can "
"be used to configure the trusted hostnames."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.http.proxy.host`"
msgstr ""

msgid "HTTP proxy host."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.http.proxy.port`"
msgstr ""

msgid "80"
msgstr ""

msgid "HTTP proxy port."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.keystore.type`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`JKS`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This property can be used to customize a keystore type if either `mp.jwt."
"verify.publickey.location` or `mp.jwt.decrypt.key.location` points to a "
"`KeyStore` file. If it is not set, the file name is checked to determine the "
"keystore type before defaulting to `JKS`."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.keystore.provider`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This property can be used to customize a `KeyStore` provider if `mp.jwt."
"verify.publickey.location` or `mp.jwt.decrypt.key.location` points to a "
"`KeyStore` file."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.keystore.password`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Keystore password. If `mp.jwt.verify.publickey.location` or `mp.jwt.decrypt."
"key.location`, this property must be set."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.keystore.verify.key.alias`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This property has to be set to identify a public verification key which is "
"extracted from `KeyStore` from a matching certificate if `mp.jwt.verify."
"publickey.location` points to a `KeyStore` file."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.keystore.decrypt.key.alias`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This property has to be set to identify a private decryption key if `mp.jwt."
"decrypt.key.location` points to a `KeyStore` file."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.keystore.decrypt.key.password`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This property can be set if a private decryption key's password in "
"`KeyStore` is different from `smallrye.jwt.keystore.password` when `mp.jwt."
"decrypt.key.location` points to a `KeyStore` file."
msgstr ""

msgid "`smallrye.jwt.resolve-remote-keys-at-startup`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set this property to true to resolve the remote keys at the application "
"startup."
msgstr ""

